<title>ITALY: Credito Bergamasco suspended from Milan bourse.</title>
<headline>Credito Bergamasco suspended from Milan bourse.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian bank Credito Bergamasco was suspended from the Milan bourse for today pending the release of a statement on the bank's future, stock market watchdog Consob said.</p>
<p>Sources close to French state-owned bank Credit Lyonnais said earlier this week that the French bank was expected to sell its 56.8 percent stake in Credito Bergamasco to Banca Popolare di Verona. Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
